// The twin of `const-fn.ya`: the same numbers, written out.
//
// Where the other program asks the compiler to compute the tables and
// carries the answers, this one spells the answers out. The two print the
// same thing and run at the same speed, which is what makes the pair a
// measurement of the `const fn` call: it costs compile time and nothing at
// run time.
fn main() {
    const squares = 338350;
    const tenth = 55;
    print(squares);
    println("");
    print(tenth);
    println("");
}
